## Summary

Fixes https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/issues/67471. A big thanks to @cshung for his help! 

What this PR does:

1. Added the ability to curate the specific GC configurations to expose to the user. 
2. Added the ability to set the configuration value used by the GC rather than that set by the user so that the most up to date and accurate information is retrieved. 
3. Provided the functionality of retrieving the appropriate configuration keys and values from the runtime to managed code by not allocating on the heap.

## Notes

- Currently the Mono and Native AOT implementations are not complete.
- A fairly simple unit test has been added as a smoke test to ensure the API works.

Current configurations that are displayed:

|Configuration Name         |Description                                                                                                                                   |
|---------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|Server GC                  |Turning on/off Server GC.                                                                                                                     |
|Heap Count                 |Number of Heaps to be created.                                                                                                                |
|Background GC              |Enabling BGC.                                                                                                                                 |
|NoAffinitize               |Affinitizing GC threads with Processors.                                                                                                      |
|Heap Affinitize Mask       |Specifies the exact processors that GC threads should use.                                                                                    |
|Heap Affinitize Ranges     |Specifies the list of processors to use for GC threads.                                                                                       |
|CPU Groups                 |Configures whether the garbage collector uses CPU groups or not.                                                                              |
|Heap Hard Limit            |Specifies the maximum commit size, in bytes, for the GC heap and GC bookkeeping.                                                              |
|Heap Hard Limit SOH        |Specifies the maximum commit size, in bytes, for the GC heap and GC bookkeeping for the SOH.                                                  |
|Heap Hard Limit LOH        |Specifies the maximum commit size, in bytes, for the GC heap and GC bookkeeping for the LOH.                                                  |
|Heap Hard Limit POH        |Specifies the maximum commit size, in bytes, for the GC heap and GC bookkeeping for the POH.                                                  |
|Heap Hard Limit Percent SOH|Specifies the allowable GC heap usage as a percentage of the total physical memory for the SOH.                                               |
|Heap Hard Limit Percent LOH|Specifies the allowable GC heap usage as a percentage of the total physical memory for the LOH.                                               |
|Heap Hard Limit Percent POH|Specifies the allowable GC heap usage as a percentage of the total physical memory for the POH.                                               |
|High Memory Percent        |Memory load Threshold to consider as a percentage of physical memory.                                                                         |
|RetainVM                   |Configures whether segments that should be deleted are put on a standby list for future use or are released back to the operating system (OS).|
|Large Pages                |Specifies whether large pages should be used when a heap hard limit is set.                                                                   |
|LOH Threshold              |Specifies the threshold size, in bytes, that causes objects to go on the large object heap (LOH).                                             |
|ConserveMemory             |Configures the garbage collector to conserve memory at the expense of more frequent garbage collections and possibly longer pause times.      |
|LatencyMode                |The period of time during which the garbage collector is active is referred to as its latency.                                                |
|GCRegionRange                | Specifies the range for the GC heap for regions.                                               |
|GCRegionSize                   | Specifies the size for a basic GC region.                                                             |

## Testing

A simple console app was used to test this functionality with the following code:

```csharp

using System.Reflection;
public partial class Program
{
    public static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        MethodInfo enumerateConfigValuesMethod = typeof(GC).GetMethod("GetConfigurationVariables", BindingFlags.Public | BindingFlags.Static);
        if (enumerateConfigValuesMethod == null)
        {
            Console.WriteLine("Incorrect version of the runtime used!");
        }
        else
        {
            Dictionary<string, object> results = (Dictionary<string, object>)enumerateConfigValuesMethod.Invoke(null, Array.Empty<object>());
            foreach (var result in results)
            {
                Console.WriteLine("{ " + $"{result.Key} : {result.Value?.ToString()}" + " }");
            }
        }
    }
}
```

The output: 

```
{ ServerGC : False }
{ ConcurrentGC : True }
{ RetainVM : False }
{ NoAffinitize : False }
{ GCCpuGroup : False }
{ GCLargePages : False }
{ LOHThreshold : 85000 }
{ HeapCount : 0 }
{ LatencyMode : -1 }
{ GCHeapAffinitizeMask : 0 }
{ GCHeapAffinitizeRanges :  }
{ GCHighMemPercent : 0 }
{ GCHeapHardLimit : 0 }
{ GCHeapHardLimitPercent : 0 }
{ GCRegionRange : 274877906944 }
{ GCRegionSize : 4194304 }
{ GCHeapHardLimitSOH : 0 }
{ GCHeapHardLimitLOH : 0 }
{ GCHeapHardLimitPOH : 0 }
{ GCHeapHardLimitSOHPercent : 0 }
{ GCHeapHardLimitLOHPercent : 0 }
{ GCHeapHardLimitPOHPercent : 0 }
{ GCConserveMem : 0 }
```

